From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vayu: log kills that make no crash report (EXIT lines)

SIGKILL from jetsam, RunningBoard or launchd and abort_with_reason without
a crash report left nothing in the sweet log, so a vanished keyboard
(InputUI) could not be explained. Prints
  EXIT name[pid] sig N status S reason ns NS code C: description
---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
index 9519bb5..5cd2570 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_exit.c
@@ -2055,6 +2055,25 @@ proc_prepareexit(proc_t p, int rv, boolean_t perf_notify)
 		corpse_source = vm_map_is_corpse_source(get_task_map(task));
 	}
 
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+	/*
+	 * vayu (sweet 0164): log kills that make no crash report (SIGKILL from
+	 * jetsam / RunningBoard / launchd, abort_with_reason without a report).
+	 * Core-signal crashes are logged as CRASH below.
+	 */
+	if ((WIFSIGNALED(rv) && !hassigprop(WTERMSIG(rv), SA_CORE)) ||
+	    (PROC_HAS_EXITREASON(p) && !hassigprop(WTERMSIG(rv), SA_CORE))) {
+		char *desc = PROC_HAS_EXITREASON(p) ?
+		    exit_reason_get_string_desc(p->p_exit_reason) : NULL;
+		printf("EXIT %s[%d] sig %d status %d reason ns %u code 0x%llx: %s\n",
+		    p->p_comm, proc_getpid(p), WIFSIGNALED(rv) ? WTERMSIG(rv) : 0,
+		    WIFSIGNALED(rv) ? 0 : WEXITSTATUS(rv),
+		    PROC_HAS_EXITREASON(p) ? p->p_exit_reason->osr_namespace : 0,
+		    PROC_HAS_EXITREASON(p) ? p->p_exit_reason->osr_code : 0ULL,
+		    desc != NULL ? desc : "(none)");
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/*
 	 * Generate a corefile/crashlog if:
 	 *      The process doesn't have an exit reason that indicates no crash report should be created
